  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A rectangle has length $x$ and width $y$ with a perimeter of $8$ units. Find its maximum area.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4$ square units, attained when $x=y=2$ units.\n\nThe area is $4-(x-2)^2$, which cannot exceed $4$.",
      "worked": "The perimeter gives $2x+2y=8$, so $x+y=4$ and $y=4-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=xy\\\\A&=x(4-x)\\\\A&=-x^2+4x\\\\A&=-(x^2-4x+4)+4\\\\A&=-(x-2)^2+4\\\\A&\\leq4.\\end{align*}$$\nEquality holds when $x=y=2$, which satisfies the perimeter constraint. The maximum area is $4$ square units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
